  "articleBody": "Blending drywall texture over a repair is an art. When done incorrectly, the patched spot stands out like a sore thumb. Here are five frequent mistakes to avoid when hiring or planning texture work.\n\n- Texturing over an uneven patch: If the base drywall patch is not sanded flat, the texture simply highlights the underlying bump or depression.\n- Skipping the test board: Applying compound directly to your wall without testing the spray density, air pressure, or trowel angle leads to mismatched patterns.\n- Stopping abruptly at repair edges: Ending texture abruptly creates a harsh perimeter line rather than a soft, feathered transition.\n- Texturing over damp compound: Skipping the 24 to 48 hour curing window traps moisture, causing bubbling, cracking, or flaking texture later.\n- Painting before primer cures: Applying paint directly over raw, unprimed texture leads to uneven sheen flashing and paint failure.\n\nWhat Can Change the Right Choice\nThe pattern type—such as orange peel, skip trowel, or heavy knockdown—determines the exact tools and compound viscosity required. To restore your walls with professional texture repairs and interior painting, contact Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 today.",
